[{:db/id "q-75832/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "294dfcb7-bdaf-5a95-8a74-13259c3185f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75832/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "14fe2aa3-6163-5eb0-930b-8f7304f87eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75832/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "7f8f096d-c958-504d-89c3-b044a8399e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75832/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "a4cc340a-eb97-5670-bf4e-8eabcde19bbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75832/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "f7b4f9f9-3f99-563e-bee5-09b39040d4f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75832/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf66df6-87fa-53e7-8d28-476241693f2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75832/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer-field/choices ["q-75832/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-75832/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-75832/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-75832/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" "q-75832/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75832" :question/id #uuid "33a013a9-ba3a-57f2-9361-b990abac67ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-75832" :question/problem "The following table gives the values of functions $g(x)$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({g}^{-1})^{′}(7).$\n\n| **$x$** | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-6$ | $9$ | $-1$ |\n| $4$ | $7$ | $-4$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({g}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}({g}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=7,$ we have\n\n$$\n({g}^{-1})^{′}(7)=\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}({g}^{-1}(7))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${g}^{-1}(7)=4$ and ${g}^{′}(4)=-4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({g}^{-1})^{′}(7) & =\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}({g}^{-1}(7))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{g}^{′}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75832/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75832"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-75986"] :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4).$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(0).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(0)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(0) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =0 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe discard $x=0$ since the logarithm is not defined here. Therefore, ${f}^{-1}(0)=5.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(5),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4)+\\frac{x}{x-4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(5) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5-4)+\\frac{5}{5-4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(5) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284/selection/b2c69c3faf1d101a6d930b3e2ac7551c72c8d4aeb34390614364ad5894868dc0" :answer/id #uuid "18e14d21-b6c3-5982-a761-c3ddc12633b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{44}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "a576bfeb-f50e-5d34-b75d-b4f735112802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "00fd7ea9-c5cf-5491-8b4d-07208bb52a63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284/selection/72eb7e0a461bb9fc7907bc78d74eec145cb690ecaaa4a5bd0d83226d3e8efeb5" :answer/id #uuid "1c5b4e62-b0ab-5606-a50e-773260737de5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "00f0cf9c-938f-5535-8a8f-976a1870e794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0307a327-bfa9-5d9e-af9a-20a228fb4cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110284/selection/72eb7e0a461bb9fc7907bc78d74eec145cb690ecaaa4a5bd0d83226d3e8efeb5" :answer-field/choices ["q-110284/selection/b2c69c3faf1d101a6d930b3e2ac7551c72c8d4aeb34390614364ad5894868dc0" "q-110284/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-110284/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-110284/selection/72eb7e0a461bb9fc7907bc78d74eec145cb690ecaaa4a5bd0d83226d3e8efeb5" "q-110284/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110284" :question/id #uuid "b4e4e308-8907-50e5-ac2c-e0df07b3b6b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-110284" :question/problem "The following table gives the values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(3)$ of the product of functions.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $-3$ |\n| $-2$ | $3$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $2$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nUsing this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function ${f}^{-1}(x)g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(x)=\\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}+{g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(3)=\\frac{g(3)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}+{g}^{′}(3){f}^{-1}(3).\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(3)=-2,$ $g(3)=-1,$ ${g}^{′}(3)=-3,$ and ${f}^{′}(-2)=-5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1}\\cdot g)^{′}(3) & =\\frac{g(3)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}+{g}^{′}(3){f}^{-1}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{{f}^{′}(-2)}+(-3)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{-5}+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110284/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer/id #uuid "1aba46c3-a1db-57c3-a68f-5042be559f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "af31f27e-8dd0-5ad0-b54b-9190421b3bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "9cc808bf-2179-5e7b-a79d-c5ea3ac5270d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "37445c44-a558-548e-b880-ae365bd0f358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d7efbf48-9657-5d03-90a0-8c5167d4dfc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5861a3c0-d5a2-5dcc-b42d-0b4f16c4e9c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110347/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-110347/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" "q-110347/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-110347/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-110347/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-110347/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110347" :question/id #uuid "db615c68-58b9-59cf-a49b-080adcb0dc8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110347" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=-3+5{e}^{x+1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(2).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(2)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(2) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =2 \\\\ -3+5{e}^{x+1} & =2 \\\\ 5{e}^{x+1} & =5 \\\\ {e}^{x+1} & =1 \\\\ x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(2)=-1.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(-1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-3+5{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =5{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =5{e}^{0} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-312581/field-1/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "6c5b27cc-72ce-5757-983e-126e34951310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-312581/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "62d7696f-552c-513c-98d7-7ef24cade1db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-312581/field-1/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer-field/choices ["q-312581/field-1/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-312581" :question/id #uuid "cebaf180-0ec8-5580-ae72-a70d7fc75656" :question/math-academy-id "q-312581" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{3x-2}{x+2}$ and the point $P(-1,-5)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ the slope of $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ at the point $(-5,-1)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(-1,-5).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{3x-2}{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{8}{(x+2)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =8\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(-1,-5)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(-5,-1)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(-5) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-5))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-312581/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e05385-7cb6-5f21-b0d8-a7641d912d5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-312581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
